VeridianOS: fix unused-variable, macro-redefinition and truncation warnings

GCC reported, with no change in behaviour needed:

- src/locking.h:37/38 "'xmalloc' redefined", "'xfree' redefined" (in every
  file that includes it after Xlibint.h): locking.h sets xmalloc/xfree to
  Xmalloc/Xfree for Xthreads.h, but Xlibint.h has usually included
  Xthreads.h already, which defaults them to malloc/free. The later
  definition already won; it now #undefs the defaults first, so the
  override is explicit. Same expansion as before.
- src/xlibi18n/lcCT.c:877 (cstoct) "variable 'unconv_num' set but not
  used": the count of dropped control characters was never returned (the
  function returns 0). Removed the counter; returning it instead would
  change what XmbTextListToTextProperty() and friends report, so the
  established result is kept.
- src/xkb/XKBGetMap.c:254 (_XkbReadKeyActions) "variable 'symMap' set but
  not used": removed the dead pointer and its increment.
- src/ErrDes.c:194 (XGetErrorDatabaseText) -Wformat-truncation: tlen is
  computed as exactly strlen(name) + strlen(type) + 2, so the snprintf of
  "%s.%s" never truncated, but GCC could not see that. The key is now
  assembled with memcpy from the lengths already computed; same string.


diff -ru a/src/locking.h b/src/locking.h
--- a/src/locking.h	2026-10-08 17:12:35.244069472 -0400
+++ b/src/locking.h	2026-10-08 17:14:22.178871693 -0400
@@ -34,6 +34,10 @@
 #ifndef _X_locking_H_
 #define _X_locking_H_
 
+/* Xthreads.h defaults these to malloc and free; it may already have been
+ * included through Xlibint.h, so replace its definitions. */
+#undef xmalloc
+#undef xfree
 #define xmalloc(s) Xmalloc(s)
 #define xfree(s) Xfree(s)
 #include <X11/Xlib.h>
